  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the&nbsp; planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> having normals <math><msub><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> respectively. The distance of the origin from the plane passing through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and whose normal is perpendicular to <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is"
  },
